-- title:
--   Stalk of the two-chart model on the j⁻¹-chart
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ with $j \neq 0$. Write $A_\infty =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, and let `XInf R F j` $= \operatorname{Spec} A_\infty$; the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of `fFin` and `fInf`, with `ιInf R F j` the morphism from $\operatorname{Spec} A_\infty$ into it and `toBase R F j` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_\infty$, i.e. a prime ideal $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ of $A_\infty$, and assume the image point $\iota_\infty(y)$ lies in the open set $\iota_\infty(\top)$. The assertion is that there is an isomorphism $e$ of commutative rings from the stalk of the structure sheaf of the two-chart model at $\iota_\infty(y)$ onto the localisation $(A_\infty)_{y.\mathrm{asIdeal}}$ such that: for every $r \in R$, $e$ sends the germ at $\iota_\infty(y)$ of the global section obtained from $r$ by the canonical identification $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R) \cong R$ followed by $\Gamma$ of `toBase R F j` to the image of $r$ under the structure map $R \to (A_\infty)_{y.\mathrm{asIdeal}}$; and for every $a \in A_\infty$, $e$ sends the germ at $\iota_\infty(y)$ of the section of the model over $\iota_\infty(\top)$ corresponding to $a$ under $A_\infty \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A_\infty)$ and the inverse of the comparison isomorphism of $\iota_\infty$ over $\top$ to the image of $a$ under $A_\infty \to (A_\infty)_{y.\mathrm{asIdeal}}$.
--
--   This is the local description of the two-chart integral model along the chart attached to $j^{-1}$: its local rings at points of that chart are the localisations of the integral closure $A_\infty$ of $R[j^{-1}]$ in $F$, with the identification compatible with both the base ring $R$ and the chart algebra. It is the $j^{-1}$-analogue of the corresponding statement for the $j$-chart, and feeds the dictionary of local rings used in the construction of normal proper models over valuation subrings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_stalk_iso_localization_chartAlgInf.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicCurve AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel

universe u

theorem AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_stalk_iso_localization_chartAlgInf
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (F : Type u) [Field F] [Algebra R F] (j : F) [Fact (j ≠ 0)]
    (y : ↥(XInf R F j))
    (hz : (ιInf R F j).base y ∈ (ιInf R F j) ''ᵁ ⊤) :
    ∃ e : (AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).presheaf.stalk ((ιInf R F j).base y) ≅
        CommRingCat.of (Localization.AtPrime y.asIdeal),
      (∀ r : R, e.hom.hom
          ((((AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).presheaf.germ ⊤ ((ιInf R F j).base y) trivial).hom
            (((toBase R F j).appTop).hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).inv.hom r)))) =
        algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime y.asIdeal) r) ∧
      (∀ a : ↥(chartAlgInf R F j), e.hom.hom
          ((((AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j).presheaf.germ ((ιInf R F j) ''ᵁ ⊤) ((ιInf R F j).base y) hz).hom
            ((((ιInf R F j).appIso ⊤).inv).hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of ↥(chartAlgInf R F j))).inv.hom a)))) =
        algebraMap ↥(chartAlgInf R F j) (Localization.AtPrime y.asIdeal) a) := by sorry
